# docs/ ships Markdown, PDF, and the diagrams the Markdown references. The
# .docx/.xlsx/.pptx sources those are generated from, and any screenshots, stay
# on the maintainer's disk — they are large, diff as binary blobs, and are not
# what a reader of the repository needs.
#
# docs/assets/ is the exception: it holds figures that README.md and the guides
# link to, so a checkout without them renders with broken images. They are
# generated by scripts/ and committed for that reason.
#
# Note what that means: ANY .png dropped into docs/assets/ is published. Put
# screenshots anywhere else — a screenshot of a settings page or a dashboard is
# exactly the kind of thing that carries an email address into a public repo.
docs/**
!docs/**/
!docs/**/*.md
!docs/**/*.pdf
!docs/assets/*.png
!docs/assets/*.svg
!docs/assets/*.gif

# Coverage output
coverage/

# Build artifacts
*.js.map
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local AI-orchestration workspace. AgentsGate is developed by dispatching
# Claude Code subagents; these hold the prompts, per-task specs and raw agent
# output that drive that loop. They are working state, not part of the shipped
# project, so they stay on the maintainer's disk and out of the repository.
CLAUDE.md
tasks/
agents/
docs/oss-release-action-items-ja.md

# Claude Code per-machine settings (permissions, enabled MCP servers)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Office lock files
~$*

# Intermediate docx text dump
docs/_docx_dump.txt
